<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end sharply down as bunds nosedive.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end sharply down as bunds nosedive.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1540 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> July 1998 6.25 pct   103.00/08 (-0.06)   bid yield 3.52 (+0.04)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		114.70/80 (-0.28)		 4.69 (+0.05)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct   100.52/60 (-0.43)		 5.68 (+0.06)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		113.45/65 (-0.75)		 6.41 (+0.05)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June)	 101.84 (-0.53)</p>
<p>TREASURIES (June)  110.09 (-0.22 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1244 (PREV 1.1244)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 -0.03     (+0.01)	 10-2 yr  216     (214)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.05     (-0.04)	 10-5 yr   99	(97)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.13     (-0.11)</p>
<p>-------------------------(May 16)-------------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds close sharply lower as they track bund futures down. Dealers say sell-off partly technical, as this week's rise on short-covering comes to end. Both rise and fall based on thin volume. Market players also careful ahead of three-day weekend and FOMC meeting on Tuesday.</p>
